MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR #80 macOS failure: 'chat with a dead primary but healthy fallback' wired
'fallback Jan (Local)' instead of the configured healthy lmstudio fallback.

Root cause (traced end-to-end):
- ConfigService is a boot-once process singleton: the daemon's preflight AND
  its provider wiring serve the config captured at the FIRST chat. The old
  test rewrote config between two chats in one process — the second chat's
  wiring never saw the rewrite.
- The wiring does not use defaults.fallbackProvider at all: routePinned
  builds the fallback chain from the intelligence catalog's RANKED
  compatible candidates. Every local preset is chat-compatible by default,
  so with ranking noise from earlier lane files, jan could outrank lmstudio
  and get wired — then fail offline on a bare runner.

Redesign (single config world, no mid-file rewrites):
- beforeAll pins THE world: primary ollama on a closed port (instant
  refusal), configured fallback lmstudio on an in-process stand-in server
  (fixed port, health flag — no socket churn), providerEngine.routingStrategy
  primary, and every other local runtime HARD-removed from the chat candidate
  set via model-level chat capability overrides (provider-level overrides do
  not propagate to model descriptors; the evaluator reads models).
- 503 test flips the stand-in down (instant 500s), invalidates the health
  caches so preflight probes live, asserts the honest 503, flips back.
- fallback test invalidates caches and asserts 200 + 'fallback reply'.
- Removes the home2/handler2 config-rewrite dance that never reached the
  booted app.

Verified: boot-profile+daemon-routes 17/17 x3; full test/perf segment
114/114 x2; core lane 257/257 files; security 309/0; reliability 70/0;
e2e 48/0; perf gate PASS; mutation PASS; tsc clean; 14 static gates exit 0.
